WEBVTT

00:01.793 --> 00:03.586
Juzo Ogami.

00:03.670 --> 00:07.549
A member of Z.O.O., the industry's
third-ranked old-guard organization.

00:08.216 --> 00:11.094
Formerly the number one
hitman in the business

00:11.177 --> 00:13.680
until he vanished without warning.

00:13.763 --> 00:15.890
Mission success rate... 100%.

00:16.391 --> 00:21.312
However, he refuses any job targeting
women, children or civilians.

00:21.896 --> 00:24.149
Preferred cigarette brand... Blue Apple.

00:24.232 --> 00:26.025
Whiskey of choice... Laphroaig.

00:27.068 --> 00:28.194
Hmm...

00:28.862 --> 00:33.783
Marksmanship, hand-to-hand combat,
knife fighting, all first-rate.

00:33.867 --> 00:36.911
Weapon of choice... the P210.

00:36.995 --> 00:41.041
He's ambidextrous, and even
when he uses a handgun with his left hand

00:41.124 --> 00:43.209
it's said to be
as accurate as a sniper's rifle.

00:43.293 --> 00:45.795
That's how it ended up nicknamed
"the Devil's Left Hand."

00:47.922 --> 00:49.215
No way.

00:54.471 --> 00:55.972
Almost there.

00:56.056 --> 00:59.976
SATURDAY, MAY 30TH

02:38.616 --> 02:42.120
So, it ends before I even use
my real weapon.

02:42.203 --> 02:43.329
How anticlimactic!

02:56.593 --> 02:58.678
So, have we contacted their parents?

02:58.761 --> 02:59.721
Not yet.

02:59.804 --> 03:01.973
Word is, someone upstairs
is holding that up.

03:03.558 --> 03:04.726
Why?

03:04.809 --> 03:05.977
Beats me.

03:06.561 --> 03:08.688
RYO SHIRAISHI
ARE YOU EATING DINNER WITH YOUR FRIENDS?

03:08.771 --> 03:09.731
LET'S SEE...

03:10.940 --> 03:14.485
All three of you, come back safe!

03:19.657 --> 03:22.744
Naturally, I'm gonna beat
the shit outta you!

03:26.080 --> 03:27.332
He's good.

03:27.415 --> 03:30.126
A straight shoot-out
puts me at a disadvantage.

03:36.925 --> 03:38.009
Good.

03:38.593 --> 03:40.094
Got my magazine back, too.

03:40.178 --> 03:42.931
Nekota's been a damn lifesaver today.

03:43.014 --> 03:44.557
Hey! Are you hurt?

03:44.641 --> 03:46.392
Huh? A-A security guard?

03:46.476 --> 03:49.812
The place is closed today, you know!
How did you even get in?

03:49.896 --> 03:51.522
Uh, well...

03:51.606 --> 03:54.275
And there've been those
strange explosions going off!

03:54.359 --> 03:56.236
It's dangerous here, so get out, hurry!

03:56.319 --> 04:00.323
Dammit, I thought he'd emptied
the place out before luring me in here!

04:00.823 --> 04:03.159
Wait! You'll drag a civilian into this!

04:03.243 --> 04:05.703
That's your policy, isn't it?

04:06.454 --> 04:08.748
Means nothing to me.

04:08.831 --> 04:12.377
With their positions...
if Juzo dodges, the guard gets hit!

04:12.961 --> 04:14.671
That's low, you bastard!

04:17.548 --> 04:19.467
What... the hell?

04:24.597 --> 04:27.934
Shooting bullets out of the air
with other bullets is impossible!

04:28.017 --> 04:31.396
The only man capable
of such an inhuman trick is...

04:32.063 --> 04:34.524
Ah, now I see. It all fits.

04:34.607 --> 04:37.026
Noren Mitsuoka. Mitsuoka Pharmaceuticals.

04:37.110 --> 04:39.070
And when I looked into you...

04:39.153 --> 04:42.073
I thought it was strange for you
to have the exact same name

04:42.156 --> 04:43.408
as that legendary hitman.

04:43.491 --> 04:46.160
But the age difference was so great,
I assumed you were someone else.

04:46.786 --> 04:50.623
As hard as it is to believe, this is
no mere case of identical names.

04:50.707 --> 04:51.833
You are...

04:51.916 --> 04:54.252
Juzo Ogami himself!

04:54.335 --> 04:55.336
He figured it out?

04:55.962 --> 04:57.463
This is why I asked

04:57.547 --> 05:00.466
if you were sure you didn't wanna change
your name before enrolling!

05:00.550 --> 05:04.220
How was I supposed
to know it'd come to this?

05:04.304 --> 05:06.556
This was supposed to be a quick little

05:06.639 --> 05:09.892
"sneak into middle school
and do some internal recon" job!

05:09.976 --> 05:11.352
Yeah, it was.

05:11.978 --> 05:12.937
Wrong!

05:13.021 --> 05:18.067
I do have a connection to Juzo Ogami,
but I'm not the legendary hitman himself!

05:19.944 --> 05:20.778
I'm...

05:20.862 --> 05:22.363
My wife's out of town today.

05:22.447 --> 05:23.281
You know...

05:23.364 --> 05:24.490
You're shameless!

05:24.574 --> 05:27.493
I'm Juzo Ogami's secret love child!

05:27.577 --> 05:29.329
What are you talking about?!

05:29.412 --> 05:32.665
Well, I'm off to Tokyo
to make it even bigger! Take care!

05:33.333 --> 05:34.334
You're shameless!

05:34.417 --> 05:36.544
After he got bored
of my mother, his mistress...

05:36.627 --> 05:40.089
he found himself a younger woman
and vanished from our lives!

05:40.173 --> 05:42.341
I swore revenge against him.

05:42.425 --> 05:45.970
So, I deliberately took the same name
and chose the same path.

05:46.054 --> 05:48.806
By making a name for myself,
I knew that someday,

05:48.890 --> 05:51.934
when I finally ran into my scumbag
old man, I'd say this to his face,

05:52.769 --> 05:55.563
"Why the hell did you abandon us?"

05:56.230 --> 05:59.192
There are so many holes
in this story, old man!

06:01.110 --> 06:02.445
I see.

06:02.987 --> 06:04.322
- I understand.
- Huh?

06:04.405 --> 06:07.075
You've had a hard life, too, haven't you?

06:07.158 --> 06:08.326
He bought it?

06:08.409 --> 06:09.494
I know how you feel!

06:09.577 --> 06:13.331
For those of us in the underworld,
life is full of misery!

06:13.414 --> 06:17.126
And the people we cross paths with?
Every last one of them is scum!

06:17.210 --> 06:19.545
Boss, you just got classified as scum.

06:19.629 --> 06:22.048
You must want to murder
your father something fierce!

06:22.131 --> 06:23.800
Y-Yeah.

06:23.883 --> 06:27.178
Well, we brothers have had
our share of troubles, too.

06:27.261 --> 06:31.224
Long ago, my younger brother Eiji
wasn't the silent type he is now.

06:31.307 --> 06:33.142
Is "silent" really the word for that?

06:35.520 --> 06:38.272
Until we were swept up
in a certain incident,

06:38.356 --> 06:40.650
I was just a kid who loved magic tricks.

06:40.733 --> 06:43.444
My brother was just a kid
who loved sports.

06:43.528 --> 06:45.822
We were no different
from any other brothers.

06:48.324 --> 06:49.408
Did you see that?

06:49.492 --> 06:50.493
My shot just now!

06:50.576 --> 06:52.703
I saw it! Nice one!

06:55.164 --> 06:56.582
Oops.

06:57.125 --> 07:00.795
Getting sentimental
won't do either of us any good.

07:01.379 --> 07:06.342
Anyway, my little brother Eiji is the most
precious person in the world to me.

07:07.301 --> 07:11.180
Noren is going to become
part of his happiness.

07:11.848 --> 07:13.224
And the secrets of Mitsuoka

07:13.307 --> 07:16.352
may even hold the possibility
of restoring my brother to his old self.

07:17.395 --> 07:19.480
Seems we both have our reasons...

07:19.981 --> 07:22.316
but I cannot afford to lose.

07:24.152 --> 07:25.278
A lighter?

07:25.361 --> 07:29.157
I told you, didn't I?
My specialty is hypnosis.

07:29.240 --> 07:33.077
And this is my true weapon.

07:42.545 --> 07:44.088
So, that's the deal!

07:44.172 --> 07:47.008
The security guard just happened
to show up at the perfect time

07:47.091 --> 07:49.051
because he was already
under this guy's control!

07:49.135 --> 07:50.470
Sorry about this!

07:56.934 --> 07:58.936
Okay, sure, gave me a little scare.

07:59.020 --> 08:00.271
But that's all you got?

08:00.354 --> 08:03.107
One civilian puppet is no sweat.

08:03.941 --> 08:06.402
One? Oh, no, no.

08:06.486 --> 08:10.072
Did you think I only started
using hypnosis after declaring war?

08:10.656 --> 08:11.949
Wrong.

08:12.033 --> 08:15.077
I knew you would make it this far.

08:15.870 --> 08:18.998
The preparations were already complete.

08:19.081 --> 08:20.124
CALLING...

08:21.000 --> 08:23.503
A long, long time ago!

08:29.634 --> 08:30.510
Don't tell me...

08:48.319 --> 08:49.487
TENMA TENDO
CALLING...

08:49.570 --> 08:51.822
Oh, Ogami? Where are you?

08:51.906 --> 08:54.242
Sorry. I got careless!
Get out of there right now!

08:54.825 --> 08:56.911
And stay away
from any crowds of civilians!

08:56.994 --> 08:58.663
They're under hypnosis!

08:58.746 --> 09:00.456
Yeah? Okay. Got it.

09:00.540 --> 09:03.709
That was way too casual! Do you
actually understand what I'm saying?

09:03.793 --> 09:05.169
I said I got it.

09:05.920 --> 09:09.590
After seeing stuff like those exploding
golf shots, I know this isn't normal.

09:10.383 --> 09:12.176
And yeah, I know I might die.

09:13.344 --> 09:14.929
But I won't run away.

09:15.012 --> 09:15.888
You little...

09:16.472 --> 09:18.808
Don't underestimate athletes.

09:19.392 --> 09:22.645
In any pro sport, the top-tier guys
may not literally be risking their lives,

09:22.728 --> 09:25.439
but they put their lives
on the line anyway.

09:26.357 --> 09:30.194
I'm aiming to be a super-elite
triple threat phenom, remember?

09:30.278 --> 09:34.699
If I can't cross one or two or three lines
between life and death, what good am I?

09:36.075 --> 09:37.952
So, yeah, I'll leave your end to you.

09:38.035 --> 09:38.869
Huh?

09:38.953 --> 09:39.745
Hey!

09:39.829 --> 09:43.124
This is risky,
but it's also a chance for me.

09:43.749 --> 09:46.961
I'm aiming to become a triple threat
Superman to pull off something

09:47.044 --> 09:49.171
completely beyond common sense.

09:49.255 --> 09:52.883
And to do that, I've given my all
to everything I could possibly need

09:52.967 --> 09:58.306
in the most efficient way possible
based on common sense and solid theory.

09:58.889 --> 10:00.141
I've gotten results.

10:00.224 --> 10:02.101
I don't think I've been wrong.

10:02.727 --> 10:05.855
But, to accomplish something
that defies common sense...

10:05.938 --> 10:09.275
I've also had the feeling I might
need something that goes beyond it.

10:10.067 --> 10:11.902
So, this is a chance.

10:11.986 --> 10:14.572
If I can make it
through this life-and-death contest,

10:14.655 --> 10:17.533
then no matter what I face
after this, I'll be able to say,

10:19.118 --> 10:21.621
"Compared to that, this is nothing."

10:22.204 --> 10:23.623
I'll know it for sure.

10:23.706 --> 10:27.918
I'm absolutely going to become
a triple threat Superman!

10:42.183 --> 10:44.393
Hey, Patchwork Giant!

10:45.061 --> 10:47.146
Let's play some sports.

11:23.224 --> 11:24.892
Dine and dash... Unforgivable!

11:31.774 --> 11:34.819
All right, then! Let's kick this off!

11:47.998 --> 11:49.750
Holy crap, this is scary!

11:49.834 --> 11:52.294
Yeah, he's an evil creep
who kidnaps people,

11:52.378 --> 11:55.798
but he's also seriously firing exploding
golf balls at me! Is he nuts?

11:56.674 --> 11:57.758
Huh?

11:57.842 --> 11:59.093
"Whock"?

12:01.303 --> 12:02.138
Huh?

12:03.764 --> 12:05.141
How'd it come from behind me?

12:05.224 --> 12:07.601
No, wait, in golf, that's...

12:08.394 --> 12:09.645
a backspin!

12:14.567 --> 12:15.609
I knew it!

12:15.693 --> 12:17.486
He switched clubs!

12:18.654 --> 12:20.781
A full set? Since when?

12:33.127 --> 12:36.464
Man, that's insane! He's hitting them
with those skinny little sticks

12:36.547 --> 12:39.717
and can curve them however he wants,
then drop 'em exactly where he's aiming?

12:39.800 --> 12:40.968
Fine then!

12:59.153 --> 13:01.322
Get back here...

13:07.495 --> 13:09.455
D-Dammit!

13:14.043 --> 13:15.711
There are too many of them!

13:15.794 --> 13:19.089
I'm worried about Tenma, but I can't go
to him with this mob in tow!

13:19.173 --> 13:20.966
Right now, all I can do is run!

13:33.270 --> 13:35.481
Crap! I ended up outside!

13:42.238 --> 13:44.406
Looks like somebody called it in.

13:44.490 --> 13:46.325
I mean, yeah, with this much commotion...

13:46.408 --> 13:48.077
No, hang on.

13:49.662 --> 13:50.996
That's not it.

13:52.540 --> 13:53.541
Take this!

13:53.624 --> 13:55.084
They're hypnotized, too?

13:56.585 --> 13:59.380
That is not what a stretcher is for!

13:59.463 --> 14:01.090
Open up the hose!

14:02.132 --> 14:03.050
Boss!

14:03.133 --> 14:05.469
No, actually, this helps.

14:09.306 --> 14:10.516
Mind if I borrow that?

14:13.852 --> 14:14.979
Sorry about this!

14:18.148 --> 14:20.109
Good thing it's not
the middle of winter, huh?

14:20.192 --> 14:21.151
Yeah.

14:21.235 --> 14:22.611
Little cold...

14:22.695 --> 14:24.405
but wake the hell up!

14:35.749 --> 14:38.043
Okay. That takes care of things for now.

14:38.878 --> 14:40.963
You did it, Boss!

14:42.339 --> 14:43.215
Big Sis?

14:43.299 --> 14:45.718
W-What the heck do you have there?

14:45.801 --> 14:48.971
No, uh, it's not real!
It's an airsoft gun! Airsoft!

14:49.555 --> 14:51.557
But what are you doing here?

14:51.640 --> 14:53.434
I came because I was worried!

14:53.517 --> 14:57.438
More importantly, what is all this?
The whole place is wrecked!

14:58.022 --> 15:00.441
But anyway, just look at this!

15:05.529 --> 15:06.947
I will count to three.

15:07.031 --> 15:10.034
When I finish counting
and you hear the lighter close,

15:10.117 --> 15:14.788
you will be unable to attack
Kazuma or Eiji Rindou.

15:16.123 --> 15:17.082
Three...

15:17.625 --> 15:18.584
two...

15:19.168 --> 15:20.085
one.

15:26.425 --> 15:27.259
You bastard!

15:27.343 --> 15:28.636
You're Kazuma Rindou?

15:29.511 --> 15:32.222
Disguises are another specialty of mine.

15:32.306 --> 15:36.018
Though I must say, it took you
an awfully long time to notice.

15:36.685 --> 15:39.813
I can't believe the boss
got caught off guard by this!

15:39.897 --> 15:41.732
This isn't like him!

15:41.815 --> 15:42.983
No, wait...

15:43.067 --> 15:44.485
it's the opposite, actually!

15:44.568 --> 15:46.695
Things ended up this way
because he acted exactly like himself!

15:46.779 --> 15:49.782
If he only had to beat down villains,
he'd be invincible!

15:49.865 --> 15:51.825
But he doesn't lay a hand on civilians!

15:51.909 --> 15:54.787
He might be a little frosty,
but he's not heartless!

15:54.870 --> 15:58.332
If anything, deep down, he's so kind
you'd never believe he was a hitman!

15:58.415 --> 16:01.418
Lately, he's even started
getting attached to his classmates!

16:01.502 --> 16:03.754
That soft side of his...

16:03.837 --> 16:07.591
played right into Kazuma Rindou's
hands in the worst way!

16:10.594 --> 16:12.554
He got me dead to rights
with that hypnosis!

16:12.638 --> 16:14.014
I really can't shoot him!

16:14.098 --> 16:17.309
Um, maybe the safety's on or something?

16:18.560 --> 16:19.853
Like hell!

16:19.937 --> 16:22.022
Don't suddenly go full idiot on me!

16:30.739 --> 16:33.033
Yeah, that figures.

16:39.915 --> 16:42.334
I can still fire in a direction
that has nothing to do with you.

16:42.418 --> 16:43.836
So, yeah, I'm definitely under.

16:44.461 --> 16:46.005
I would not recommend that.

16:46.088 --> 16:49.049
Don't blame me if a stray bullet
hits somebody random.

16:51.552 --> 16:53.012
Well, whatever.

16:53.095 --> 16:54.555
That's just about the right handicap.

16:54.638 --> 16:57.683
Guess it's time to show you
just how different our careers really are.

16:57.766 --> 16:58.934
Wha...

17:00.227 --> 17:01.395
Wha...

17:06.108 --> 17:07.568
He hid.

17:07.651 --> 17:09.486
But the outcome will be the same.

17:10.195 --> 17:14.324
I can't finish him off with just
my Walther, even while he's hypnotized.

17:14.825 --> 17:17.161
That bullet-shooting trick is a nuisance.

17:17.911 --> 17:18.871
Very well.

17:18.954 --> 17:22.708
I'll lay one more trap
and see how he responds!

17:26.336 --> 17:29.840
Come on out, Ogami's love child!

17:30.966 --> 17:32.885
Right, that was the story!

17:34.636 --> 17:37.890
You can see what this means, right?
Come out within three seconds.

17:37.973 --> 17:41.268
You have a policy against
involving civilians in this, don't you?

17:42.644 --> 17:45.230
There was still
another hypnotized civilian?

17:45.314 --> 17:47.441
Also, what kind of hostage choice is that?

17:48.150 --> 17:49.735
Doesn't this picture look backward?

17:51.361 --> 17:53.113
Fine, fine. I'm coming.

17:53.781 --> 17:55.157
There you are.

17:55.240 --> 17:56.742
Throw your gun over here.

17:59.787 --> 18:02.081
Would you like to hear this man scream?

18:02.164 --> 18:03.582
P-Please help me!

18:10.422 --> 18:14.593
Honestly, was that poor aim
or one last little act of spite?

18:17.513 --> 18:18.555
Now, then...

18:19.389 --> 18:21.767
do you have any last words?

18:22.768 --> 18:24.603
Yeah. I'm begging you.

18:26.522 --> 18:29.274
Take off that disguise.

18:33.737 --> 18:34.988
Very well.

18:39.201 --> 18:41.036
Satisfied?

18:41.537 --> 18:43.413
Then... die--

18:43.497 --> 18:44.498
Oh, that's a relief!

18:44.581 --> 18:45.707
Thanks!

18:45.791 --> 18:47.292
Even knowing it was fake,

18:47.376 --> 18:50.629
I wasn't crazy about punching
somebody wearing Big Sis's face.

18:50.712 --> 18:51.505
Huh?

18:52.422 --> 18:54.842
Now you'd better grit your teeth.

19:00.430 --> 19:01.431
Wha...

19:01.515 --> 19:03.475
A sniper? An ally?

19:03.559 --> 19:05.561
No, the bullet came from directly above!

19:05.644 --> 19:06.812
Huh? It can't be!

19:06.895 --> 19:09.314
That stray shot from before?

19:12.776 --> 19:14.403
Wait, did you actually aim that?

19:14.486 --> 19:17.489
Because if he did,
that is not humanly possible!

19:17.573 --> 19:20.909
I figured out the trick messing around
during training back in the day.

19:20.993 --> 19:24.079
Well, it's not like shooting normally.

19:24.163 --> 19:26.832
My hit rate's only about 70%
on a good day.

19:26.915 --> 19:28.959
That is still not humanly possible!

19:29.042 --> 19:29.877
Again!

19:29.960 --> 19:32.171
I was aiming for the stretcher.

19:32.254 --> 19:35.465
I fired three shots,
so I figured one of 'em would hit.

19:36.049 --> 19:38.760
And at the foot of the stretcher
is a detonator.

19:38.844 --> 19:43.849
Lock picks, mini bombs
and a bunch of useless...

19:43.932 --> 19:47.561
When I hid a minute ago,
I set both of them up.

19:47.644 --> 19:49.188
Oh, got it!

19:49.271 --> 19:51.148
So, what's gonna happen?

19:51.231 --> 19:53.108
Just watch.

19:53.192 --> 19:55.360
What have you been
muttering about over there?

20:00.949 --> 20:02.576
And what is that supposed to be?

20:03.243 --> 20:06.246
I said I was gonna beat
the shit outta you, remember?

20:06.330 --> 20:09.416
I wanted to do it full force from my end

20:09.499 --> 20:10.834
but, well, whatever.

20:10.918 --> 20:13.837
You can come over here
and take your beating.

20:19.176 --> 20:20.219
Wha...

22:15.250 --> 22:16.335
You...

22:16.835 --> 22:18.712
I can't believe it!

22:18.795 --> 22:22.966
Is this what you predicted would happen
when you fired into the sky?

22:23.050 --> 22:25.260
Hmm? Well, roughly.

22:25.927 --> 22:28.680
When I fired,
I was only aiming for the stretcher.

22:28.764 --> 22:31.516
After that, I calculated
backward as I moved.

22:33.101 --> 22:38.106
I mean, that's how I can explain it, but I
wasn't thinking it through that precisely.

22:38.190 --> 22:40.317
It was half-assed. Totally winging it.

22:40.400 --> 22:42.444
What is he?

22:43.236 --> 22:45.322
It isn't just that he's skilled!

22:45.405 --> 22:47.407
The sheer amount of experience...

22:47.491 --> 22:49.201
the depth of his strength...

22:49.868 --> 22:51.620
He's in a different league!

22:54.706 --> 22:56.541
But it's too late now!

22:56.625 --> 22:57.459
What?

22:57.542 --> 23:01.296
Noren Mitsuoka is already hypnotized.

23:01.963 --> 23:07.219
When she wakes, she will fall in love
with the first person she sees!

23:07.302 --> 23:08.220
What?

23:08.303 --> 23:09.387
Dammit!

23:09.930 --> 23:11.598
